quran[24]{c,v,t}:
  51,7,"By the sky full of galaxies and pathways (of planets and stars),"
  51,8,"indeed, you are (lost) in conflicting opinions."
  51,9,Only he is turned away (from the Qur’an) who has been deluded.
  51,10,"Ruined are those who tell lies out of conjecture,"
  51,11,those steeped in ignorance and are neglectful (of the Hereafter).
  51,12,They ask (mockingly): ‘When is the Day of Retribution?’
  51,13,(Say:) ‘It is the Day (when) they will be tormented over the Fire.’
  51,14,(And they will be told:) ‘Taste your torment. This is what you sought to hasten.’
  51,15,"Indeed, the pious will be (rejoicing) in gardens and springs."
  51,16,"Receiving (delightfully) what their Lord has granted them, for they had been virtuously excellent before that."
  51,17,They used to sleep only a little during the night.
  51,18,And they would seek forgiveness in the latter part of the night (i.e. before dawn).
  51,19,"And in their wealth, there was a rightful share for the beggar and the deprived."
  51,20,"Upon the earth, there are signs for those with sure faith,"
  51,21,and within yourselves (as well). Do you not then perceive?
  51,22,And in the heaven is your sustenance and whatever you are promised.
  51,23,"By the Lord of the heaven and the earth, this (promise) is surely true, just as (the fact that) you can speak."
  51,24,Did the story of the honoured guests of Ibrahim (Abraham) reach you?
  51,25,"When they (i.e. the angels) entered his presence, they greeted him with: ‘Peace!’ He (also) said (to them): ‘Peace (be upon you)!’ (Addressing himself, he said:) ‘They are unfamiliar people.’"
  51,26,Then he went quietly to his family and brought out a fat (roasted) calf.
  51,27,He placed it before them and said: ‘Will you not eat?’
  51,28,"(When they did not eat,) he started becoming fearful of them. They (i.e. the angels) said: ‘Do not be afraid.’ And they gave him the glad tidings of a knowledgeable son (Ishaq [Isaac])."
  51,29,"Then his wife (Sara) came up with a loud cry (in joy), patting her forehead in wonder and said: ‘(What!) A barren old woman (giving birth to a child)?’"
  51,30,"They (i.e. the angels) said: ‘Such has your Lord decreed. Indeed, He is the All-Wise, the All-Knowing.’"
